hnique to inject RokRat. Retrieved March 22, 2022.", "source_name": "Malwarebytes RokRAT VBA January 2021", "url": "https://blog.malwarebytes.com/threat-analysis/2021/01/retrohunting-apt37-north-korean-apt-used-vba-self-decode-technique-to-inject-rokrat/"}], "id": "relationship--cfc92bbe-4a8b-47ec-b12d-d08fdcea1fbb", "modified": "2026-04-29T14:23:06.209Z", "object_marking_refs": ["marking-definition--fa42a846-8d90-4e51-bc29-71d5b4802168"], "relationship_type": "uses", "revoked": false, "source_ref": "malware--60a9c2f0-b7a5-4e8e-959c-e1a3ff314a5f", "spec_version": "2.1", "target_ref": "attack-pattern--354a7f88-63fb-41b5-a801-ce3b377b36f1", "type": "relationship", "x_mitre_attack_spec_version": "3.3.0", "x_mitre_deprecated": false, "x_mitre_modified_by_ref": "identity--c78cb6e5-0c4b-4611-8297-d1b8b55e40b5"}', 'kb-doc-09-mitre-attack-p0-17204', 0, 219, '09-mitre-attack', 'retrieved', 'FE45040FFEF61D55FE0DC09BB68644B58C1BE2B8A7AEC9EEC8C5AD336CAA472D', 'v1', '{"source_id": "09-mitre-attack", "version": "retrieved", "corpus_version": "v1", "knowledge_object_type": "STRUCTURED_DATA"}')
